  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With no completed experiments, there is zero evidence about which design dimensions matter. The most important initial uncertainty is whether the core multimodal fusion hypothesis holds at all. Config_001 (multimodal, singleprofile, scgpt + imagenet_vit_l, concat) is the cleanest baseline multimodal configuration: it pairs the strongest available RNA encoder (scgpt, a pretrained scRNA-seq foundation model) with the strongest image encoder (ViT-L pretrained on ImageNet), uses the simplest profile setting (singleprofile, so no aggregation is needed), and applies the most straightforward fusion (concat). This isolates the question 'does combining these two strong unimodal representations yield a useful multimodal model?' without confounding from multiprofile aggregation, learned fusion weights, or weaker encoders. If it performs well, the next experiment can be a single-modality baseline (e.g., image-only or RNA-only) to quantify the multimodal benefit. If it underperforms, we can decompose whether the issue is encoder choice, fusion strategy, or the modality combination itself. Starting here gives the most information per experiment under a limited budget."
}

